{
  "$schema": "../../level.schema.json",
  "id": "6.8",
  "chapter": 6,
  "number": 8,
  "title": "Boss: the new laptop",
  "concept": "Clone, commit, push, handle a rejection, end in sync",
  "boss": true,
  "story": [
    {
      "speaker": "Sam",
      "text": "My old laptop died. I have a new one and nothing on it."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Ada",
      "text": "You are on the new laptop now. Do the whole round trip yourself."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Ada",
      "text": "Get the project, add the contact page, and get it online."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Ada",
      "text": "I am editing the README at the same time, so expect a bump."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Ada",
      "text": "No hints on the steps this time. You have done every piece already."
    }
  ],
  "workdir": "~",
  "setup": {
    "steps": [
      {
        "hosted": {
          "id": "lantern-labs/festival-site",
          "description": "The Lantern Labs festival website",
          "visibility": "public",
          "defaultBranch": "main",
          "collaborators": [
            "ada-okafor",
            "sam-builds"
          ],
          "initialFiles": {
            "index.html": "<h1>Lantern Festival</h1>\n",
            "README.md": "The Lantern Labs festival website\n",
            "schedule.html": "<h2>Saturday</h2>\n"
          },
          "initialMessage": "Festival site so far",
          "initialAuthor": "Ada Okafor <ada@lanternlabs.example>"
        }
      },
      {
        "machineAdd": {
          "id": "newlaptop",
          "label": "New laptop",
          "host": "newlaptop"
        }
      },
      {
        "switchMachine": "newlaptop"
      }
    ]
  },
  "teammates": [
    {
      "id": "ada-edits-readme",
      "when": {
        "on": "commands",
        "count": 3
      },
      "actions": [
        {
          "type": "say",
          "speaker": "Ada",
          "text": "Heads up, I just pushed a line to the README."
        },
        {
          "type": "push",
          "actor": "ada-okafor",
          "repo": "lantern-labs/festival-site",
          "branch": "main",
          "message": "Mention the parade in the README",
          "files": {
            "README.md": "The Lantern Labs festival website\nSaturday night lantern parade.\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "goal": {
    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Get the project onto the new laptop",
        "checks": [
          {
            "type": "repoExists",
            "machine": "newlaptop",
            "repoPath": "~/festival-site"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Commit a contact page",
        "checks": [
          {
            "type": "fileExists",
            "machine": "newlaptop",
            "path": "~/festival-site/contact.html"
          },
          {
            "type": "commitExists",
            "changes": [
              "contact.html"
            ],
            "machine": "newlaptop",
            "repoPath": "~/festival-site"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Keep Ada's README change too",
        "checks": [
          {
            "type": "fileContent",
            "machine": "newlaptop",
            "path": "~/festival-site/README.md",
            "contains": "parade"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The website has everything and you are in sync",
        "checks": [
          {
            "type": "hostedFile",
            "repo": "lantern-labs/festival-site",
            "path": "contact.html"
          },
          {
            "type": "inSync",
            "machine": "newlaptop",
            "repoPath": "~/festival-site",
            "branch": "main"
          },
          {
            "type": "clean",
            "machine": "newlaptop",
            "repoPath": "~/festival-site"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "par": 6,
  "allowedCommands": null,
  "hints": [
    "There is nothing on this computer yet. Start by getting the project, then work normally.",
    "Clone, cd into the folder, create and commit contact.html, then push. If the push is refused, pull and push again.",
    "`git clone https://github.com/lantern-labs/festival-site.git`, `cd festival-site`, make contact.html, `git add contact.html`, `git commit -m \"Add contact page\"`, `git push`, then `git pull` and `git push`."
  ],
  "questions": [],
  "recap": "You did the full round trip: clone, commit, push, and recover from a rejected push with pull. That is the everyday loop of working with other people.",
  "glossary": [],
  "cheatSheet": [],
  "predict": null,
  "ui": {
    "panels": {
      "hub": true,
      "remote": true
    },
    "hubPage": "lantern-labs/festival-site"
  },
  "solution": [
    {
      "run": "git clone https://github.com/lantern-labs/festival-site.git"
    },
    {
      "run": "cd festival-site"
    },
    {
      "run": "echo \"<p>Email hello@lanternlabs.example</p>\" > contact.html"
    },
    {
      "run": "git add contact.html"
    },
    {
      "run": "git commit -m \"Add contact page\""
    },
    {
      "run": "git push"
    },
    {
      "run": "git pull"
    },
    {
      "run": "git push"
    }
  ]
}
